## Handling 404 Routes

Every app needs a fallback for unknown routes. Use a wildcard (`*`) path to catch unmatched routes.

```jsx
// src/App.js
<Routes>
  <Route path="/" element={<Home />} />
  <Route path="/about" element={<About />} />
  <Route path="/products" element={<Products />} />
  <Route path="/products/:productId" element={<ProductDetail />} />
  <Route path="*" element={<NotFound />} />
</Routes>
```

```jsx
// src/components/NotFound.js
function NotFound() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>404 - Page Not Found</h2>
      <p>The page you're looking for doesn't exist.</p>
      <Link to="/">Go to Home</Link>
    </div>
  );
}

export default NotFound;
```

- The `*` path matches any unmatched route.
- Always include a 404 page for better UX.

> ✅ Accessibility: Ensure your 404 page includes a link back to the homepage and has proper heading structure.

