## Advanced: Pathless Routes and Index Routes

React Router v6 supports **pathless routes**—routes that don’t match a URL segment but render content (e.g., for layout wrappers or error boundaries).

```jsx
<Route path="/dashboard" element={<Dashboard />}>
  <Route index element={<DashboardHome />} />
  <Route path="profile" element={<Profile />} />
  <Route path="settings" element={<Settings />} />
  <Route path="*" element={<Dashboard404 />} /> {/* Handles invalid nested paths */}
</Route>
```

- `index` route matches when the parent path is matched exactly.
- Pathless routes can wrap other routes for shared behavior.

