## Optimistic Updates

Give users instant feedback by updating the UI before the server responds—then roll back if the request fails.

### Example: Toggle Product Visibility

```jsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import axios from 'axios';

function ProductItem({ product, onUpdate }) {
  const [isVisible, setIsVisible] = useState(product.visible);
  const [pending, setPending] = useState(false);

  const handleToggle = async () => {
    // Optimistic update
    setIsVisible(!isVisible);
    setPending(true);

    try {
      await axios.patch(`/api/products/${product.id}`, {
        visible: !isVisible,
      });
      onUpdate(); // Refresh list or update cache
    } catch (err) {
      // Revert on failure
      setIsVisible(isVisible);
      alert('Failed to update visibility');
    } finally {
      setPending(false);
    }
  };

  return (
    <li>
      <span>{product.name}</span>
      <button onClick={handleToggle} disabled={pending}>
        {isVisible ? 'Hide' : 'Show'}
      </button>
    </li>
  );
}
```

> ✅ **When to use**:
> - Low-risk operations (e.g., toggles, likes)
> - Fast UI feedback improves UX
> - Rollback ensures data consistency

> ⚠️ **Avoid for**:
> - High-stakes actions (e.g., payments, deletions)
> - Long-running operations

